copyshop is source-available, not open source. Its source code is published so
you can read it, learn from it, report and fix problems, and build copyshop for
yourself. Buying copyshop at https://getcopyshop.com gets you the official
builds: signed, kept up to date, and supported.

1. What you may do

   a. Read, study and modify the source code.
   b. Build copyshop from the source code, with or without your changes, and
      run that build on your own devices, for your own use.
   c. Use your build for any work, personal or commercial. The images you make
      with copyshop are yours.
   d. Publish changes to the source code as source code (for example a fork
      or a patch on GitHub), under this same license.

2. What you may not do

   a. Share, sell, give away or otherwise distribute builds of copyshop or of a
      modified version of it, in any form: app bundles, installers, packages,
      disk images, or a version hosted on the web for others to use.
   b. Offer copyshop, or a modified version of it, to others as a product or
      a service.
   c. Use the source code, in whole or in substantial part, in another
      product.
   d. Use the copyshop name or icon for a modified version, or in a way that
      suggests it is an official build.
   e. Remove or change this license or the copyright notices.

